threads.body:
The javadoc above says only a `RemotingException` triggers this, but the check is message-text only. Any throwable escaping `getInvoker()` that happens to carry that text (for example a wrapper that chained the message) will emit a bogus `_OTHER` server span. Dubbo throws `org.apache.dubbo.remoting.RemotingException` for the exporter miss consistently across 2.7.x and 3.x, so please gate on the type too, the way `isUnknownServiceDecodeFailure` gates on `IOException`:

```java
if (!(throwable instanceof RemotingException)) {
  return false;
}
```

(needs an import for `org.apache.dubbo.remoting.RemotingException`)

