threads.body:
`_otel_unknown_svc_span` was the old attachment-based dedup key, but nothing reads it anymore now that dedup uses a `VirtualField` — the string only appears here. So this is just setting an arbitrary attachment and doesn't guard against anything specific. I'd drop it (the `RpcContext` import goes with it).

```suggestion
    try {
      genericService.$invoke("hello", new String[] {String.class.getName()}, new Object[] {"test"});
    } catch (Throwable ignored) {
      // expected: service not exported on provider
    }
```

